The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (pmd_none(*vmf->pmd) && folio_test_pmd_mappable(folio)) {
    ...
}
if (pmd_none(*vmf->pmd))
```
Reason:
The `filemap_map_pmd` function assumes that when it encounters `pmd_none`, a corresponding page table entry (PTE) has already been preallocated in `prealloc_pte`. If the PMD becomes empty while servicing a page fault, this can lead to dereferencing a NULL pointer, resulting in a kernel oops.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (pmd_none(*vmf->pmd) && vmf->prealloc_pte)
    pmd_install(mm, vmf->pmd, &vmf->prealloc_pte);
```
Reason:
The patch adds a check to ensure that `vmf->prealloc_pte` is valid before calling `pmd_install`. This prevents the function from attempting to use a NULL pointer for the PTE, thereby avoiding potential kernel oops errors when the PMD is empty.

